Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 10:53:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 056/154] feat: open a link another app hands over in a little
 window
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

-[AppController application:openURLs:] now asks the core where a handed-over
link belongs before it hands the list to the stock path. With the setting on
and every URL in the list http(s), each opens a chromeless little window;
anything else - the setting off, a mailto:/file:/javascript: URL, no resident
profile - falls through untouched with the whole list.

The decision lives in Rust (navigation::decide_external_link_target) so the
scheme rule and the setting rule are asserted without a browser. The setting is
a new settings.json key, externalLinksOpenInLittle, absent reads on. It is
seeded at startup because openURLs runs on the UI thread, where reading a file
is a fatal DCHECK, and re-applied on save so a running browser stops ignoring
the row until the next launch.

Replaces the startup_behavior target, whose last reader is gone.

IsOnCurrentWorkspace returned false, which made FindTabbedBrowser skip every
Atrium window - so the setting-off path built a second space window instead of
adding a tab. Stock BrowserView returns true on Mac; so does this now.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 chrome/browser/app_controller_mac.mm | 14 ++++++++++++--
 chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn           |  4 +++-
 2 files changed, 15 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/app_controller_mac.mm b/chrome/browser/app_controller_mac.mm
index 90313ec7137c9..a6c21aa11e143 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/app_controller_mac.mm
+++ b/chrome/browser/app_controller_mac.mm
@@ -71,6 +71,7 @@
 #include "chrome/browser/tab_group_sync/tab_group_sync_service_factory.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/task_manager/task_manager_metrics_recorder.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/atrium/atrium_dock_reopen_hook.h"
+#include "chrome/browser/ui/atrium/atrium_external_link_hook.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/browser.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/browser_command_controller.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/browser_commands.h"
@@ -2093,8 +2094,17 @@ class AppControllerProfileObserver : public ProfileAttributesStorage::Observer,
     }
   }
 
-  if (!gurlVector.empty())
-    [self openUrlsReplacingNTP:std::move(gurlVector)];
+  if (gurlVector.empty())
+    return;
+
+  // With externalLinksOpenInLittle on, a link another app hands
+  // over opens in a chromeless little window instead of a space window. False
+  // - the setting off, a non-http(s) url, no resident profile - leaves the
+  // stock path below untouched with the whole list.
+  if (atrium::HandleExternalLinks(gurlVector))
+    return;
+
+  [self openUrlsReplacingNTP:std::move(gurlVector)];
 }
 
 // Show the preferences window, or bring it to the front if it's already
